+## Per-file summary
+
+### Application (`crates/application/src/comfy_runtime`)
+- `ports.rs:63` new trait `ExtraModelPathsWriter { generate(root, base), remove(root) }` (async-trait, separate from `ExtraModelPaths`; read-only consumers and their fakes are untouched).
+- `model.rs:198` new `RuntimeError::ExtraPathsRejected(String)` (`#[error("{0}")]`).
+- `use_cases.rs:311` `ManageExtraModelPaths::new(root: Arc<dyn RootSwitcher>, writer: Arc<dyn ExtraModelPathsWriter>)` with `generate(&Path)` and `remove()`; the root is `root.current().root` on every call. `RootSwitcher` is the existing root provider (`EnvironmentDeps.root`).
+- `tests.rs:488-` `RecordingWriter` fake and `manage_extra_model_paths_uses_the_current_root` (asserts the root `/install` for generate and remove, the base is forwarded, and an `ExtraPathsRejected` passes through unchanged).
+
+### Infrastructure (`crates/infrastructure/src/comfy_runtime`)
+- `extra_paths.rs:1-14` module doc, `mod writer;`, `pub use writer::APP_SECTION;`. The reader is unchanged.
+- `extra_paths/writer.rs` (new) implements `ExtraModelPathsWriter for YamlExtraModelPaths` (blocking work in `spawn_blocking`).
+  - `generate` (`:91`): `checked_base` -> `<root>/ComfyUI` must exist -> `outside_app_folders` -> `reject_links` -> `load` the existing file (validated before anything is created) -> `create_folders` -> build the section -> back up when the old file's first line is not the app header -> `atomic_write`.
+  - `remove` (`:117`): same safety loading; no-op when the file or section is missing; backs up a not-app-written file before changing it; deletes the file when no section remains; never touches folders.
+  - Section (`app_section`, `:306`): `base_path`, `is_default: false`, then keys sorted/de-duplicated case-insensitively = the 18 section 4.6 names + `configs` + existing `ComfyUI/models` subfolders that are valid `SafeFileName`s, do not start with `.`, and are not `clip`/`unet` (also skipped: `base_path`, `is_default`). Values are `<name>/`; `text_encoders` adds `clip/`, `diffusion_models` adds `unet/` (joined with `\n`) only if that directory exists under the base. Emitted with `serde_yaml_ng`; first line is the exact header text.
+  - Existing file (`load`, `:243`): refuses with `extra_model_paths.yaml could not be updated safely: {reason}. Edit or move it, then retry.` for link/not-a-regular-file, > 1 MiB, non-UTF-8, malformed YAML, non-mapping top level (null/empty/comment-only = empty mapping), and any `<<` key at the top level or in a section. Other sections are kept as data in their original order; the app section is replaced in place or appended.
+  - Backup (`back_up`, `:368`): `<root>/data/backups/extra_model_paths-<YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ>.yaml` via `create_new` (a same-second collision gets `-1`, `-2`, ...); never beside the original.
+  - Validation messages are the exact strings from the plan (constants `:52-58`).
+- `extra_paths/writer/tests.rs` (new): the nine Rust tests below.
+
