+2. Use case `ManageExtraModelPaths::new(EnvironmentDeps-or-the-existing-root-provider, Arc<dyn ExtraModelPathsWriter>)` with `generate(base)` and `remove()`; the root comes from the current root provider (`root.current()` as other use cases do). Wire the writer into the desktop runtime adapters and the use case into the comfy services. New error `RuntimeError::ExtraPathsRejected(String)` → IPC code `extra_model_paths_invalid` (message passed through; it never contains secrets) with an error-mapping test.
+3. Commands `comfy_generate_extra_model_paths { basePath: string }` and `comfy_remove_extra_model_paths` (manager window only; ACL + permissions + bindings + acl.rs cases). After a successful write, trigger the existing library rescan (`services.library.rescan` or equivalent); rescan errors are logged only.
+4. File semantics (infrastructure `extra_paths.rs`, writer side):
+   - App section key `vjumpkung_desktop`. File's first line: `# Managed by vjumpkung ComfyUI desktop. Other sections are kept; the vjumpkung_desktop section is rewritten by the app.`
+   - Section: `base_path` = the user's absolute path (trailing separators removed, never a `\\?\` form), `is_default: false`, then keys sorted and de-duplicated case-insensitively = the REQUIREMENTS §4.6 primary names (`checkpoints, diffusion_models, text_encoders, vae, loras, controlnet, clip_vision, embeddings, upscale_models, latent_upscale_models, style_models, hypernetworks, photomaker, gligen, audio_encoders, model_patches, vae_approx, diffusers`) plus `configs`, plus every existing subfolder of the install's `ComfyUI/models` that is a valid `SafeFileName`, does not start with `.`, and is not `clip` or `unet`. Each value `<name>/`; `text_encoders` gets a second line `clip/` only if `<base>/clip` is a directory, `diffusion_models` gets `unet/` the same way (multi-line value joined with `\n`).
+   - Create missing primary folders under the base (`create_dir_all` for the base itself, `create_dir` per category); if a FILE with a category's name exists → refuse; existing folders (and links) are left as they are.
+   - Emit with `serde_yaml_ng` (correct quoting for spaces/Thai); write with `crate::shared::fs::atomic_write`.
+5. Existing file: refuse with "extra_model_paths.yaml could not be updated safely: {reason}. Edit or move it, then retry." when it is a link/reparse point, > 1 MiB, not UTF-8, malformed YAML, the top level is not a mapping (null/empty counts as empty mapping), or any section contains a `<<` merge key. Otherwise keep the other sections as data (comments are lost). If the file exists and its first line is not the app header, first copy it to `<root>/data/backups/extra_model_paths-<YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ>.yaml` (create `data/backups`; never write a backup next to the original — ComfyUI's `.gitignore` covers only `extra_model_paths.yaml`, a sibling would dirty the checkout and block app updates). `remove()` deletes only the app section and deletes the file when no section remains; it never deletes folders; a missing file/section is a no-op success.
+6. Validation (fail closed, `ExtraPathsRejected` with these exact messages): not absolute, or a `\\?\` / `\\.\` form → "Choose an absolute folder path on a local drive or network share."; contains `$` or `%` or starts with `~` → "The folder path must not contain $ or % and must not start with ~, because ComfyUI expands them."; control characters → same as the first message; equal to the install root or inside `<root>/ComfyUI`, `<root>/envs`, `<root>/data`, `<root>/tools` (compare after canonicalizing the nearest existing ancestor; case-insensitive on Windows) → "Choose a folder outside the app's ComfyUI, envs, data and tools folders."; any existing prefix component is a link/junction (reuse `reject_reparse` from `crate::shared::model_paths`) → "The folder or one of its parents is a link or junction. Choose the real folder."; `<root>/ComfyUI` missing → "ComfyUI is not installed yet."
+7. UI (`comfy-page.tsx` card, extract a component file in the same feature folder if the card grows; kebab-case file name): input "Model base folder" + Browse (`gateway.pickFolder`), buttons **Generate** and **Remove generated section** (enabled only when the read list contains a root with section `vjumpkung_desktop`). Description replaces "Read-only.": "Choose a model base folder and the app writes a section that adds every model folder inside it, creating missing folders. ComfyUI/models stays the default location, and app downloads still go there." While ComfyUI is running show "Restart ComfyUI to use the new paths." after a successful change. Refetch the extra-paths list and library after success; show errors from the IPC message.
+8. Tests (exact names) — Rust: `generate_writes_a_managed_section_and_creates_missing_folders`, `generate_preserves_other_sections_and_backs_up_a_hand_written_file` (backup in `data/backups`, original content byte-equal in the backup), `regenerate_is_idempotent_and_makes_no_new_backup`, `remove_deletes_only_the_app_section_and_the_file_when_empty`, `legacy_alias_lines_are_added_only_when_the_folder_exists`, `generate_refuses_unsafe_base_paths`, `generate_refuses_a_file_it_cannot_rewrite_safely`, `generated_file_round_trips_through_the_reader` (the existing parser returns exactly the expected roots, incl. a base path with a space and Thai characters), `#[cfg(windows)] generate_refuses_a_junction_in_the_base_prefix` (create via `cmd /C mklink /J`; skip if unavailable like other junction tests), `manage_extra_model_paths_uses_the_current_root` (application), ACL + error-mapping cases. Vitest: `generates_with_the_chosen_folder_and_refreshes_the_list`, `remove_is_offered_only_for_the_app_section`, `shows_restart_hint_while_comfyui_runs`.
+9. Docs (only these): `docs/DOCUMENTATION.md` model library / ComfyUI section — how to generate, what is written, backups in `data/backups`, `is_default: false`, limitation "app downloads still go to ComfyUI/models", ComfyUI must be restarted; `docs/REQUIREMENTS.md` FR-COMFY-8 — append "Implemented: the app manages its own `vjumpkung_desktop` section from a chosen base folder; other sections are kept."
+
